  "notes": "South Central, but assigned to boom-bap rather than g-funk because the material is a sampled record and not a synth band — that is the section's own assignment rule. The research documents a shift rather than a style, so this is two modes: `bizarre-ride` is J-Swift's sampledelic bounce, quantised at 0.82 with bright major-7th colour, and `labcabin` is the Dilla feel, quantised at 0.62 with 12–14ms of timing jitter and the snare pushed 7ms late — \"kick early, snare dragging\" as parameters rather than as prose. Four voices trading is why `melody.densityPerBar` is [4,8] and `countermelody.densityRatio` is 0.6 in a section whose other jazz entries sit near 0.4. Harmony is the real thing: ii–V–I and I–vi–ii–V with `ninth` at 0.38 for the major-7th and 9th colour. ⚠ \"The bass lands slightly behind the kick\" has no dedicated parameter, so in the `labcabin` mode it is carried by `humanize.timingJitterMs` and a lowered `anticipationProb` — an approximation, and named as one. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
